<p class="lesson-lead">
    Last day before Winter Break! Yesterday your friends playtested your boss cold and handed you a
    list of real problems. Today you <strong>revise</strong> the top blockers, verify every fix on
    a fresh playtest run, freeze changes cleanly, and showcase your finished game before break.
</p>

<!-- ============================================================ -->
<div class="activity basic-app">
    <div class="activity-header">
        <span class="activity-label">In the Editor + Code: Revise &amp; Re-Verify (~35 min)</span>
        <span class="activity-time">~35 min</span>
    </div>

    <p>
        Work strictly top-down from your <a href="8.5.html">8.5</a> playtest notes. A clean,
        complete boss fight beats an ambitious broken build every time:
    </p>

    <ol>
        <li><strong>Fix Bugs &amp; Soft-Locks first:</strong> any crash, missing <code>"Ground"</code> tag, stuck collider, or non-resetting hazard after <code>StatManager.Die()</code> gets fixed immediately.</li>
        <li><strong>Fix Confusion second:</strong> clarify where to stand, how to hurt the boss (e.g., hit flash, Console/UI feedback, clear weak point), and how to exit/win once HP hits zero.</li>
        <li><strong>Tune Numbers third:</strong> adjust <code>health</code>, <code>speed</code>, <code>timeBetweenShots</code>, or <code>cooldownTimer</code> only after bugs and confusion are solved.</li>
        <li><strong>Verification Re-Test (mandatory!):</strong> ask one of yesterday's testers (or a new classmate) to replay ONLY to verify that your top revision actually solved the problem they ran into.</li>
        <li><strong>Build Freeze &amp; Smoke Check:</strong> press Play starting from <code>Start (index 0)</code> → <code>Overworld</code> → <code>Platformer</code> → Boss → Victory (plus one intentional death test). Commit and push cleanly with a clear commit message.</li>
    </ol>

    <div class="socratic">
        <h3>Socratic: Revising with Discipline</h3>
        <ol>
            <li>Write down the specific complaint from yesterday's friend playtest, the exact change you made today (script line, prefab setting, or scene layout), and what happened when a tester re-played it.</li>
            <li>What feature or visual polish did you intentionally <em>cut</em> today so the core boss loop stays bug-free before break?</li>
            <li>If you tweak one more number ("just one quick buff to speed") five minutes before showcase WITHOUT re-playing the whole fight, what risk do you create?</li>
        </ol>
    </div>
</div>

<!-- ============================================================ -->
<div class="activity basic-app">
    <div class="activity-header">
        <span class="activity-label">Class Showcase: Play &amp; Celebrate (~25 min)</span>
        <span class="activity-time">~25 min</span>
